- Thread-Safe Asset Referencing: Dynamic spawning queues for mobs, vehicles, and dungeon layouts must utilize safe pointer validation checks to prevent race conditions or null-pointer crashes if a chunk unloads while an asset is still instantiating.

## 27.2 EXCEPTION HANDLING & FALLBACK SAFEGUARDS
- Missing Asset Fallbacks: If a procedural generation call requests an asset or material tag that fails to load or is missing from the directory, the engine must inject a default fallback placeholder mesh rather than crashing the game instance or breaking the execution loop.
- Coordinate Overflow Protection: Long-distance traversal tracking across massive 20,000-mile environments must implement floating-point origin rebasing (world origin shifting) to prevent physics jitter, collision degradation, and precision loss at extreme world coordinates.



